{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D11", "D12", "D36"],
      "pins": ["D11.2", "D12.2", "D36.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0037"],
      "observed": "The anodes (pin 2 = \"A\") of the three Ethernet status LEDs D11, D12 and D36 are tied together on net /NET0037, which has no other nodes — no connection to +3V3, 3.3V_PI_OUT or any other supply rail. Their cathodes (pin 1 = \"K\") go through R70/R35/R57 to the CM4 open-drain pins Ethernet_nLED3 (Module2.15), PI_nLED_Activity (Module2.21) and Ethernet_nLED2 (Module2.17). By contrast every other discrete status LED on the board has its anode tied to a supply (e.g. D9.2 and D38.2 sit on +3V3 via R69/R60, D5.2 sits on +3V3 via R69).",
      "expected": "The common-anode net for the Ethernet LEDs should be connected to a positive supply (e.g. +3V3, matching the other status LEDs), so that when the CM4 nLED pin sinks current the LED conducts. A common-anode node left floating cannot supply any current.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"11\") (name \"/NET0037\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D11\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D12\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D36\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"157\") (name \"Net-(D11-K)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D11\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R70\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") (class \"Med Power\") ... (node (ref \"D9\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... )"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The three Ethernet link/activity LEDs can never illuminate because their common anode has no supply connection; the board loses its Ethernet status indication even though the CM4 drives the cathode side correctly.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R46"],
      "pins": ["R46.1", "R46.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R46's value field is \"24k\" (SPICE also models it as 24k), but its own description and MPN say 24 ohm: description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\" and MPN \"FRC0805J240TSD\" (240 = 24Ω). R46 sits across VOUTP/VOUTN, the Bob-Smith/common-mode termination nodes fed by the D27/D47 bridge rectifiers.",
      "expected": "The value field and the ordering metadata (description/MPN) should describe the same resistance. In a 75Ω Bob-Smith termination network a 24Ω bleed would load the network heavily, so one of the two numbers is wrong.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R46\") (value \"24k\") (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R46 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the board is assembled from the BOM (24Ω) rather than the schematic value (24k), the VOUTP/VOUTN network is about 1000x lower in resistance than the schematic intends, loading the Ethernet common-mode termination and the Q4/R88/R101/D33/D34 sense network.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an apparent open connection: the anodes of the three Ethernet status LEDs (D11/D12/D36) are tied only to each other on net /NET0037 and to no supply rail, so those LEDs cannot light; a secondary inconsistency exists in R46 whose value (24k) disagrees with its description/MPN (24Ω)."
}

